[ ] Apply a charter's defaults to its actions =charter-defaults $A charter's own frontmatter describes the charter; its defaults map gives values to descendant actions that set none. Spec which keys apply and how a default meets an ancestor action's inherited window, which can only narrow. Core today only projects defaults. Promotion writes the children's inherited conditions there.$ !3 ^2026-11-25T03:50 #01a210d3-1d94-7f90-a835-8acb619eff5f
[ ] Rename a charter and its alias from the CLI =rename-charter $Changing a charter's alias today means a frontmatter edit that leaves its file name and plan collection on the old stem. One verb renames a charter: alias, stem and directory together, moving its files, sidecar and plans/ collection, keeping its id, and safe to interrupt as archive is. Promotion's generic subcharter-NN aliases depend on it being cheap.$ !3 ^2026-11-25T03:53 #01a210d5-f4d6-7302-a18c-cbb1af61fc75
